  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "The temple of the goddess Gula, Esabad (\u201cHouse of the Open Ear\u201d), was located in the Tuba district of Babylon, in the western half of the inner city. According to the Babylonian topographical text Tintir = Babylon Tablet IV, it was one of three temples in that part of Babylon. Esabad was rebuilt by the Assyrian king Ashurbanipal (r. 668\u2013ca. 631 BC) and Nebuchadnezzar II (r. 604\u2013652 BC). The temple survived into Arsacid times (247\u00a0BC\u2013AD 224).",
